PipeWire
========

url    = https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/pipewire/pipewire.git
tag    = 1.6.11
commit = 4287f31510771fc999f8a58a024c81ca10b8d55f
date   = 2026-10-29

tools/desktop/build-pipewire.sh builds this revision (GitLab's archive of
the tag, identical to the submodule, checked by SHA-256) with
tools/desktop/patches/pipewire-dragonfly.txt and installs it in
/System/Library/PipeWire, with epoll-shim built against eventfd(2) and
WirePlumber (contrib/wireplumber). Only the JACK backend is built: the
sound goes through the JACK tunnel to jackd on OSS
(docs/desktop-pipewire.md). Keep build output outside the submodule; when
upgrading, update the tag and checksum in build-pipewire.sh too.

License: see COPYING, LICENSE and individual file notices. Complete the
file-level and asset provenance review and preserve applicable notices and
source obligations before distribution.

When upgrading, review dependencies, API and ABI compatibility, FoxynBSD
portability (the patch), license notices and the full desktop build and
runtime tests, including the audio check.
